{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall not plant for yourself an asherah.</b> It is joined here to say that justice requires that the judge begin by investigating public idolatry first. Here Rashi explained: a warning to one who plants a tree, etc. — that is, from <b>לא תטע</b> we derive 'one who plants a tree.' And from <b>כל עץ</b> we derive 'one who builds a house' — that is, from 'any tree,' even detached, and ultimately he joined it." "<b>Beside the altar.</b> For this is their practice, to make for yourself an asherah beside an altar of idolatry, as is explained in the passage of Gideon. And furthermore, so that it not appear, when they come to sacrifice at the altar, as if they are coming to worship the asherah, as it is written: ואשריהם על עץ רענן."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:08.022940545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}